{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-36010" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $f(x)=|x-2|+1,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\n- $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$\n- $x\\in (1,\\infty )$\n- $x\\in (2,4]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/state.json" "file_sha256" "60c9ec2447e0a8c63511815926cf884c324ee68bec4f5a1c40375a0616337b84"} {"question" "q-36010" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The graph of the function $f(x)=|x-2|+1$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n- Take the curve $y=|x|.$\n\n- Translate it by $2$ units to the right,  to get $y=|x-2|.$\n\n- Finally, translate $y=|x-2|$ by $1$ unit up to get $f(x)=|x-2|+1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/ceab1637313ae53869cc1e59f6a56ad6cb920a83dffba482558b696188df0d36.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$ and $x\\in (2,4].$ On these intervals, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/a47169838785b6f4ac78253252bcedc3c2cb752a655feac9945e20dd40563b4f.png)\n\n  \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (1,\\infty ).$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/14ed35294e1179ffd9efaf87fa8ac1eb99853a7da344e462c2cb0dda74c3b78f.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/state.json" "file_sha256" "60c9ec2447e0a8c63511815926cf884c324ee68bec4f5a1c40375a0616337b84"} {"question" "q-36010" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fb7b55d60138fc43d6ab866786df3f437bc8a9a5e48d6944bea7a51119f8ee9a"} {"question" "q-36010" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/state.json" "file_sha256" "60c9ec2447e0a8c63511815926cf884c324ee68bec4f5a1c40375a0616337b84"} {"question" "q-36010" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/state.json" "file_sha256" "60c9ec2447e0a8c63511815926cf884c324ee68bec4f5a1c40375a0616337b84"} {"question" "q-36010" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/state.json" "file_sha256" "60c9ec2447e0a8c63511815926cf884c324ee68bec4f5a1c40375a0616337b84"} {"question" "q-36039" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/936cea1e20ef7bbc1eb66acf9dd564c61476f5bb68ee05e553b00aaf3f970dc3.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible? \n\n- $x\\in [-4,0]$\n- $x\\in (-4,-2]$\n- $x\\in (-3,1)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/state.json" "file_sha256" "60c9ec2447e0a8c63511815926cf884c324ee68bec4f5a1c40375a0616337b84"} {"question" "q-36039" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.  \n\n- The given function is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in [-4,0]$ and $x\\in (-4,-2].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/a4499c2d4995c09b9ab6f8852cc2982f415f1650d65429c86df83800344106f4.png)\n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval $x\\in (-3,1]$  because some lines will intersect the curve at more than one point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/cb0a462b3af10d15bb586f127baac45a74eecd5dc19848bda23664e75de968a4.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/state.json" "file_sha256" "60c9ec2447e0a8c63511815926cf884c324ee68bec4f5a1c40375a0616337b84"} {"question" "q-36039" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fb7b55d60138fc43d6ab866786df3f437bc8a9a5e48d6944bea7a51119f8ee9a"} {"question" "q-36039" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/state.json" "file_sha256" "60c9ec2447e0a8c63511815926cf884c324ee68bec4f5a1c40375a0616337b84"} {"question" "q-36039" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/state.json" "file_sha256" "60c9ec2447e0a8c63511815926cf884c324ee68bec4f5a1c40375a0616337b84"} {"question" "q-36039" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/state.json" "file_sha256" "60c9ec2447e0a8c63511815926cf884c324ee68bec4f5a1c40375a0616337b84"} {"question" "q-36934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/1eccd6630b69558f8a86f8336e9f0e49f37ffb29acf4a3c8f58be34346b4c93c.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\n- $x\\in [-2,0]$\n- $x\\in (-3,-2]$\n- $x\\in (-3,-1]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/state.json" "file_sha256" "60c9ec2447e0a8c63511815926cf884c324ee68bec4f5a1c40375a0616337b84"} {"question" "q-36934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in [-2,0]$  and $x\\in (-3,-1]$ because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/d8cc826df6fed7a4106539d88ffa8a1fdc0529904497c2d5413f9761acaccd12.png)\n\n        \n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-3,-2].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/bc00ed8f4bdf03b248dbd9a1651ed073e352d512b830139505fba3b60e05e7e9.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \" II only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/state.json" "file_sha256" "60c9ec2447e0a8c63511815926cf884c324ee68bec4f5a1c40375a0616337b84"} {"question" "q-36934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fb7b55d60138fc43d6ab866786df3f437bc8a9a5e48d6944bea7a51119f8ee9a"} {"question" "q-36934" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/state.json" "file_sha256" "60c9ec2447e0a8c63511815926cf884c324ee68bec4f5a1c40375a0616337b84"} {"question" "q-36934" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "II  only"] ["text" "III only"] ["text" "None"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/state.json" "file_sha256" "60c9ec2447e0a8c63511815926cf884c324ee68bec4f5a1c40375a0616337b84"} {"question" "q-36934" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II  only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/state.json" "file_sha256" "60c9ec2447e0a8c63511815926cf884c324ee68bec4f5a1c40375a0616337b84"} {"question" "q-66729" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $f(x)=|x-1|-2,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\n- $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$\n- $x\\in (1,\\infty )$\n- $x\\in (-\\infty ,2]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/state.json" "file_sha256" "60c9ec2447e0a8c63511815926cf884c324ee68bec4f5a1c40375a0616337b84"} {"question" "q-66729" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The graph of the function $f(x)=|x-1|-2$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n- Take the curve $y=|x|.$\n\n- Translate it by $1$ units to the right,  to get $y=|x-1|.$\n\n- Finally, translate $y=|x-1|$ by $2$ units down to get $f(x)=|x-1|-2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/753840da17642582f9dbc0debc18f1fa3efcbbb11142894c1dd823ad6c0c630a.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$ and $x\\in (1,\\infty ).$ On these intervals, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/15f1c797cbddd2ac8e2e9c5be72f842e7d1accfc5f619af57b1f35a27e1015c0.png)\n\n  \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,2].$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/a100489b49da7b06c98783b1b1c4ec0de9d891fc2b22f4b36b1a0ac2d54fc4f3.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I  and II only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/state.json" "file_sha256" "60c9ec2447e0a8c63511815926cf884c324ee68bec4f5a1c40375a0616337b84"} {"question" "q-66729" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fb7b55d60138fc43d6ab866786df3f437bc8a9a5e48d6944bea7a51119f8ee9a"} {"question" "q-66729" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/state.json" "file_sha256" "60c9ec2447e0a8c63511815926cf884c324ee68bec4f5a1c40375a0616337b84"} {"question" "q-66729" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/state.json" "file_sha256" "60c9ec2447e0a8c63511815926cf884c324ee68bec4f5a1c40375a0616337b84"} {"question" "q-66729" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/state.json" "file_sha256" "60c9ec2447e0a8c63511815926cf884c324ee68bec4f5a1c40375a0616337b84"} {"question" "q-108667" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/811ead4928d2f245235736dce473d121261ea358ca4ff3a0cc8b01bb2e9f3b31.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\n- $x\\in (-3,3)$\n- $x\\in [1,4]$\n- $x\\in (-\\infty ,-3]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/state.json" "file_sha256" "60c9ec2447e0a8c63511815926cf884c324ee68bec4f5a1c40375a0616337b84"} {"question" "q-108667" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,-3].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/32f1ad5bdec30951900a1c30c2996ea040e65880f859c43769faf374db06a2f0.png)\n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the intervals $x\\in (-3,3)$ and $x\\in [1,4]$ because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/8ed451b24fa83de513f4a1b5c79d39f94add784c6b7265e765a3381e7b03363a.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/state.json" "file_sha256" "60c9ec2447e0a8c63511815926cf884c324ee68bec4f5a1c40375a0616337b84"} {"question" "q-108667" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fb7b55d60138fc43d6ab866786df3f437bc8a9a5e48d6944bea7a51119f8ee9a"} {"question" "q-108667" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/state.json" "file_sha256" "60c9ec2447e0a8c63511815926cf884c324ee68bec4f5a1c40375a0616337b84"} {"question" "q-108667" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/state.json" "file_sha256" "60c9ec2447e0a8c63511815926cf884c324ee68bec4f5a1c40375a0616337b84"} {"question" "q-108667" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/state.json" "file_sha256" "60c9ec2447e0a8c63511815926cf884c324ee68bec4f5a1c40375a0616337b84"}] "usage" {"q-36039" []} "basis" 2331 "retractions" [[17592186124867 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1889/Source/Images/q-36039.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\n1. $x ∈ [- 4, 0]$\n2. $[MATH: x ∈ (-4,-2]]$\n3. $x ∈ (-3, 1)$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186122225 17592186122226 17592186122227 17592186122228 17592186122229] "immutable_fields" [[17592186122224 :answer-field/correct] [17592186122224 :answer-field/id] [17592186122224 :answer-field/key] [17592186122224 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
